        "original_id": "a935f377-9053-5dfc-a50b-e02fb633bf53",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Stephen James Meridith Brown, Willie Burke\n- Organizations: Central Catholic Library\n- Places: Holywood, County Down, Ireland, Kilcrony, Wicklow, Belfast Lough, Belfast, Bangor, Dublin\n- Roles: Jesuit priest, writer, bibliographer, librarian, footballer\n\nFacts:\n- Stephen James Meridith Brown was born on 24 September 1881 in Holywood, County Down, Ireland.\n- Holywood is a civil parish and townland of 755 acres on the shore of Belfast Lough between Belfast and Bangor.\n- Stephen James Meridith Brown was an Irish Catholic Jesuit priest, writer, bibliographer, and librarian.\n- Stephen Brown, S.J. founded the Central Catholic Library on 25 June 1922 to help the laity educate themselves.\n- Willie Burke was born on 4 September 1972 in Dublin.\n- Willie Burke is a former Irish footballer.\n- Stephen James Meridith Brown died on 8 May 1962 in Kilcrony, Wicklow, Ireland.",
